	<h2 _msttexthash=3D"183612" _msthash=3D"25">Description</h2><font _mstmuta=
tion=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"86598057" _msthash=3D"26"> By using the selected=
 relational database management system, you will learn and use the SELECT s=
tatement and its parts (ORDER BY, WHERE, GROUP BY and grouping functions, H=
AVING, JOINs, nested selects, set operations), SQL functions. SQL DDL state=
ments that handle tables (CREATE, ALTER, DROP, TRUNCATE). SQL DML statement=
s (INSERT, DELETE, UPDATE, MERGE). SQL DCL statements (COMMIT, ROLLBACK, SA=
VEPOINT, GRANT, REVOKE). Use other database objects. </font><h2 _msttexthas=
h=3D"204958" _msthash=3D"27">Competencies</h2>
	<ul><li _msttexthash=3D"24163022" _msthash=3D"28">He/she has basic and up-=
to-date knowledge and understands the factual material in the field of data=
bases, i.e. the basic task solving principles, methods and procedures of th=
e development and operation processes. </li><li _msttexthash=3D"6724328" _m=
sthash=3D"29">He/she is able to perform routine development tasks in the IT=
 field in the case of database management systems. </li><li _msttexthash=3D=
"24573055" _msthash=3D"30">He/she is able to use professional sources of in=
formation and to find the knowledge necessary for the problem to be solved.=
 Based on their existing knowledge, they effectively acquire new technologi=
es and paradigms.</li></ul>
